事实上，如果有的话，他觉得那天他也得到了一些东西。他是一名电影制作人，在小镇中奖的那天，他拿起摄像机去了广场。那一刻发生的时候，简直就像有人把剧本交到了我手里。他拍摄了所有的庆祝活动，从那以后他一直在拍摄。他说，看到整个城镇同时获得财富时会发生什么，这真的很有趣。整个事情就像一个有着非常快速结果的社会实验，可以研究和观察这样的事件会对人们产生什么影响。并不总是好的。

29
00:14:23.000 --> 00:15:03.000
Costa thinks the people in Sarato have become a little more insular since the win, more focused on the nuclear family and less on the town as a community. You do see how he's affecting how they have changed, how they have closed. Before that, all the doors were constantly open. The way he talks about it makes me wonder if the people in the town will like the film when they see it. But Coastie says he thinks they will, mostly. Maybe a few small things they might not like it, but that's reality.
科斯蒂斯认为，自中奖以来，索德托的人们变得更加封闭了，更关注核心家庭，而对作为社区的城镇关注较少。你确实能看到他是如何影响他们的改变，他们是如何封闭的。在那之前，所有的门总是开着的。他谈论这件事的方式让我怀疑镇上的人在看到这部电影时是否会喜欢它。但科斯蒂斯说他认为他们会，大部分会。也许有一些小地方他们可能不喜欢，但这就是现实。

30
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:37.000
One thing about Sarato, there are birds, a lot of them. Luckily this is also one of the things I'm able to say in Spanish. Pajados, sí. And yetchas. Another thing about Soretto, it's hot. Marie Carmen, the former secretary of the Housewives Association, tells me it's not usually this hot until later in the summer. This heat, she says, I just can't with this heat.
关于索德托的一件事，那里有鸟，很多鸟。幸运的是，这也是我能用西班牙语说的事情之一。鸟，是的。还有那些。关于索德托的另一件事，它很热。家庭主妇协会的前秘书玛丽卡门告诉我，通常夏天晚些时候才会这么热。她说，这种热，我真的受不了这种热。

31
00:15:37.000 --> 00:16:11.000
As we walk around, Sodeto, she's pointing out a few houses that have been fixed up with lottery money. But mostly Marie Carmen says, the town hasn't changed that much. So, that was a town of farmers and some of them installed new irrigation systems or bought new tractors. Some people made modest additions to their homes, but nothing that extravagant. Kielo, Vania, Terva. Unlike Costa's, Marie Carmen hasn't noticed the town being more closed off since the lottery. She thinks there have been some little jealousies here and there, not everyone won the same amount.
当我们走在索德托时，她指出了几栋用彩票钱修缮过的房子。但玛丽卡门说，小镇并没有太大变化。所以，那是一个农民小镇，有些人安装了新的灌溉系统或买了新的拖拉机。有些人对他们的房子进行了适度的扩建，但没有什么太奢侈的。不像科斯蒂斯，玛丽卡门并没有注意到自彩票以来小镇变得更加封闭。她认为这里偶尔会有一些小嫉妒，毕竟不是每个人赢的金额都一样。

32
00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:41.000
But overall, she thinks it's been an incredible thing for everyone in this little working-class town to live without the worry of debt. She's been battling cancer, which keeps going away and coming back, and the money's allowed her to stop working and not worry. For me personally, the lottery has just brought a sense of calm. I don't know, like, to have the day to day cover it, you know?
但总的来说，她认为对于这个小镇上的每个人来说，能够不用担心债务地生活是一件不可思议的事情。她一直在与癌症作斗争，病情反复，这笔钱让她可以停止工作，不用担心。对我个人来说，彩票只带来了一种平静感。我不知道，就像，能够应付日常开销，你知道吗？

33
00:16:41.000 --> 00:17:16.000
And that's the thing with this Syndicate-style lottery, unlike the Powerball Trackpot, which heaps hundreds of millions on one or two lonely winners. The money from the Christmas lottery gets divvied up among thousands of people, and they don't generally win enough to buy mansions and yachts. They win enough to pay off their debts, maybe buy a Honda Civic. The lottery brings wealth to a whole geographic area and distributes it relatively evenly, at least among those lucky enough to have a ticket. After a short walk, Marie Carmen and I arrive at the new office of the Housewives Association,
这就是这种联合式彩票的特点，不像强力球头奖，它将数亿美元堆在这一两个孤独的赢家身上。圣诞彩票的钱被分给成千上万的人，他们通常赢的钱不足以购买豪宅和游艇。他们赢的钱足够还清债务，也许买一辆本田思域。彩票将财富带给整个地理区域，并相对均匀地分配它，至少在那些幸运地拥有彩票的人中间是这样。走了一小段路后，玛丽卡门和我到达了家庭主妇协会的新办公室，

34
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:55.000
which now, to be more modern, is officially called the Women's Association, but everyone still seems to call it the Housewives Association. Back in 2011, when they were selling lottery tickets, the group kept for for themselves, which ended up winning them 400,000 euros. At the time, enough to cover their budget for the next 200 years. With all the new money, they fixed up an old school building in town and made it into their office slash community center. It has a nice kitchen for parties, a laundry room and a fitness center.
为了更现代化，现在正式称为妇女协会，但每个人似乎仍然称它为家庭主妇协会。回到2011年，当他们出售彩票时，该组织为自己保留了一些，最终赢得了40万欧元。当时，这足以支付他们未来200年的预算。有了这笔新钱，他们修缮了镇上的一栋旧校舍，把它变成了他们的办公室兼社区中心。它有一个漂亮的派对厨房、一个洗衣房和一个健身中心。

35
00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:31.000
You see, all of this was made with lottery money. This living room was built, the kitchen, and the association gave coasties some money for his film. We gave him... I don't remember how much, if it was 15,000 euros or how much. I don't know, it was a good bit. But she also mentions that he hasn't finished it yet, and everyone is waiting.
你看，所有这些都是用彩票钱做的。这个客厅是建的，厨房也是，协会还给了科斯蒂斯一些钱拍电影。我们给了他……我不记得是多少了，是1.5万欧元还是多少。我不知道，是一笔不错的数目。但她也提到他还没有拍完，每个人都在等。

36
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:59.000
No, it still hasn't come out in theaters or anything yet. The people here in the village are waiting, like, what's up, we gave you money. Marie Carmen isn't the only one to mention this to me. It actually seems to be the talk of the town. A little later that day I run into a group of older guys. When I tell them I met with Coasties, one of them says, The one who made the movie.
不，它还没有在电影院上映或什么的。村里的人都在等，就像，怎么回事，我们给了你钱。玛丽卡门并不是唯一一个向我提到这一点的人。这似乎成了镇上的谈资。那天晚些时候，我遇到了一群老伙计。当我告诉他们我见过科斯蒂斯时，其中一个人说，那个拍电影的人。

